  "title": "Read, watch, speak",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Learn each new verb as a pair: the **আমি** form and the **সে** form. These three verbs keep their vowel; only the ending changes:\n\n- পড়া 'read / study': আমি **পড়ি** — সে **পড়ে**\n- দেখা 'see / watch': আমি **দেখি** — সে **দেখে**\n- বলা 'speak / say': আমি **বলি** — আপনি **বলেন**\n\nThe object comes **before** the verb, never after: **আমি বই পড়ি** 'I read books', **সে টিভি দেখে** 'he watches TV'.\n\n**পড়া** means both 'read' and 'study': **আমি বাংলা পড়ি** can be 'I read Bengali' or 'I study Bengali'.\n\n**পড়ে** 'reads' sounds exactly like **পরে** 'later', which you'll meet in Lesson 7. Only the spelling differs (ড় vs র).",
  "vocab": [
